(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[19 1 "// The module _ssl (queue 209, PYS22 (a); CPython 3.14.10's Modules/_ssl.c and its clinic file) over Go's"] [20 1 "// crypto/tls: ssl.py runs unchanged on it. A context (_SSLContext) keeps OpenSSL's settings as _ssl.c reads and"] [21 1 "// writes them (options, verify mode and flags, host flags, the protocol bounds, the cipher list, ALPN, the"] [22 1 "// certificate chain and key, the trust store) and makes a tls.Config of them for each connection. An SSL object"] [23 1 "// (_SSLSocket, over a socket or a pair of MemoryBIOs) drives a tls.Conn in a goroutine of its own over an"] [24 1 "// in-memory transport (builtins_ssl_conn.go), so OpenSSL's non-blocking contract (SSL_ERROR_WANT_READ, a"] [25 1 "// handshake resumed by calling again) holds for both. Verification is _ssl's own over Go's x509 (the codes and"] [26 1 "// messages of OpenSSL's X509_verify_cert_error_string), certificates decoded as _decode_certificate does"] [27 1 "// (builtins_ssl_cert.go). What Go's TLS does not have is by design (doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"As built: 209\")."] [29 1 "// The constants as CPython 3.14.10 with OpenSSL 3.5 defines them."] [67 2 "// the py_ssl_error codes"] [78 1 "// _ssl.c's line numbers in its error messages (\" (_ssl.c:N)\"), from CPython 3.14.10's source."] [105 1 "// sslReady gives SSLCertVerificationError its two bases (SSLError, ValueError), as egReady does"] [106 1 "// ExceptionGroup's."] [118 1 "// sslError is fill_and_set_sslerror: an exception of type t, its args (code, message), the message"] [119 1 "// \"[LIB: REASON] errstr: verify (_ssl.c:LINE)\" with the parts it has, its reason and library attributes."] [150 1 "// sslPEMLib is OpenSSL's ERR_R_PEM_LIB as _setSSLError reports it."] [155 1 "// ---- the context ----"] [171 30 "// the TLS 1.2-and-below list set_ciphers selected"] [178 35 "// the Python object: an ssl.SSLContext's instance, or the context itself"] [179 35 "// one chain a key type (OpenSSL's SSL_CTX keeps one RSA, one EC ...)"] [189 1 "// sslStoreCert is a certificate of the trust store."] [194 45 "// a fallback root's (x509roots/'s distrust-after)"] [198 46 "// basicConstraints"] [206 46 "// keyUsage's keyCertSign"] [210 2 "// X509_check_ca: a version 1 self-signed certificate is a CA"] [214 1 "// addStore puts a DER certificate in the trust store (once: X509_STORE's hash table)."] [221 11 "// OpenSSL keeps what Go's parser refuses; it cannot anchor Go's verification"] [268 29 "// PY_SSL_MIN_PROTOCOL"] [277 3 "// the subclass's instance made here, so the context knows it (CPython hands the SSLContext itself to the"] [278 3 "// SNI callback and as SSLSocket.context)"] [289 1 "// sslDefaultCiphers is PY_SSL_DEFAULT_CIPHER_STRING."] [292 1 "// tlsVersions is the range of TLS versions the context allows Go: its protocol, its bounds and its OP_NO_*."] [326 1 "// ---- passwords and keys ----"] [328 1 "// sslPassword is a password argument: str, bytes or bytearray (at most PEM_BUFSIZE, 1024 bytes), or a callable"] [329 1 "// called when an encrypted key needs it."] [370 1 "// sslParseKey is a PEM file's first private key, decrypted with the password when it is encrypted."] [379 37 "//nolint: the legacy encryption of OpenSSL's traditional keys"] [589 1 "// sslDefaultPaths are OpenSSL's defaults on Linux, as get_default_verify_paths reports them."] [594 1 "// setDefaultVerifyPaths is X509_STORE_set_default_paths: the default file loaded now, the directory looked up"] [595 1 "// at verification; $SSL_CERT_FILE and $SSL_CERT_DIR replace them. When the host has no store (no certificate in"] [596 1 "// the file, no certificate file in the directories: tamago, a bare container), the checkout's x509roots/ bundle"] [597 1 "// (Mozilla's roots, with their distrust-after dates as constraints) takes its place (the user's decision on"] [598 1 "// 209's DECISION 1, (a), 2026-11-05)."] [654 1 "// SSLRoot is a root of the fallback store: its DER and, when it has one, the constraint a chain it anchors must"] [655 1 "// pass (x509roots/fallback/bundle's Root)."] [661 1 "// sslFallbackRoots is the bundle's roots, set by the package arbace/pyssl (over arbace/x509roots/fallback/bundle),"] [662 1 "// which the interpreted runtime loads the first time it is needed (so a run that verifies against the host's store"] [663 1 "// never loads the bundle's forms) and a compiled program links."] [666 1 "// SetSSLFallbackRoots is arbace/pyssl's registration of the bundle."] [669 1 "// SSLDistrustAfter is the bundle's rule for a root with a distrust-after date: every certificate of the chain"] [670 1 "// issued (NotBefore) on or before it."] [682 1 "// sslFallback is the fallback store's roots: the bundle's, or, for tests, $PYI_SSL_FALLBACK_ROOTS's (a PEM file"] [683 1 "// standing in for the bundle, a block's \"Distrust-After: RFC 3339 time\" header its constraint, as the bundle's"] [684 1 "// distrustAfter)."] [712 1 "// sslX509Roots is _ssl._x509roots(), a test function as _test_decode_cert: the fallback store's roots as"] [713 1 "// (subject, distrust-after) pairs, the date None for an unconstrained root (read back from the constraint's"] [714 1 "// message, the bundle keeping no other trace of it)."] [742 1 "// pool is the trust store as Go's verifier takes it: the store's certificates and those of the capath"] [743 1 "// directories (OpenSSL's by-hash lookup: every certificate file of the directory)."] [773 1 "// ---- ciphers ----"] [775 1 "// sslCipher is a cipher suite Go implements, under OpenSSL's name and attributes."] [779 19 "// SSL_CIPHER_get_version"] [781 19 "// OpenSSL's Kx= and Au= words"] [782 19 "// Enc="] [783 19 "// Mac="] [786 21 "// the cipher-string words that select it"] [795 1 "// sslCiphers are Go's TLS 1.0-1.2 suites in OpenSSL's default order."] [845 1 "// sslSelectCiphers evaluates an OpenSSL cipher string over sslCiphers (ssl_cipher_process_rulestr's operators:"] [846 1 "// ':' ',' ' ' separate, '+' joins words, '!' kills, '-' removes, a leading '+' moves to the end, \"@STRENGTH\","] [847 1 "// \"@SECLEVEL=N\"); false when no cipher is selected."] [911 1 "// sslCipherDict is cipher_to_dict."] [935 1 "// sslCipherTuple is cipher_to_tuple: (name, protocol, bits)."] [940 1 "// ---- the module ----"] [1264 20 "// Go's TLS has no finite-field DHE: the parameters are read and not used"] [1433 2 "// The OpenSSL API level the port follows (ssl.py and the tests branch on it): 3.5.0, the release CPython"] [1434 2 "// 3.14.10's references ran with; the text says what implements it."] [1475 20 "// Go's crypto/rand needs no seeding"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[198 39] [206 39] [256 53] [270 42] [338 22] [344 49] [346 31] [430 53] [439 56] [461 40] [509 58] [514 58] [519 26] [530 36] [534 39] [544 35] [565 51] [573 35] [579 33] [601 23] [604 23] [608 32] [616 28] [627 33] [647 58] [686 45] [694 39] [695 45] [730 29] [732 38] [764 48] [966 41] [1000 24] [1018 24] [1054 106] [1074 88] [1079 88] [1083 90] [1187 23] [1271 29] [1273 38] [1316 30] [1457 28] [1467 29] [1468 36] [1472 32] [1492 33]] :go/trails [[792 113] [813 168] [1402 103] [1417 57] [1428 64]]} (go/file "builtins_ssl.go" :imports [


